ch the nebula's gases shine most intensely; at other wavelengths the glow fades almost entirely\"}", "result": "Key 'observation method' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "The topic is astronomy.", "Pictor Nebula": "Located about four thousand light-years away, is an emission nebula where young stars pour radiation into surrounding gas making it glow, embedded stars heat the gas cloud, and gravity slowly pulls gas together until stars ignite", "star formation process": "Gravity pulls gas together, making cloud hotter and denser until star ignites", "observation method": "Scientists observe with an optical telescope tuned to red light, the frequency at which the nebula's gases shine most intensely; at other wavelengths the glow fades almost entirely"}}]}, "final_kv": {"topic": "The topic is astronomy.", "Pictor Nebula": "Located about four thousand light-years away, is an emission nebula where young stars pour radiation into surrounding gas making it glow, embedded stars heat the gas cloud, and gravity slowly pulls gas together until stars ignite", "star formation process": "Gravity pulls gas together, making cloud hotter and denser until star ignites", "observation method": "Scientists observe with an optical telescope tuned to red light, the frequency at which the nebula's gases shine most intensely; at other wavelengths the glow fades almost entirely"}, "recall_raw": "Question 1: 1,2,3\nQuestion 2: 1,2\nQuestion 3: 1,2\nQuestion 4: 1\nQuestion 5: 5\nPassage Difficulty: 6\nQuestion Difficulty: 7", "parsed_answers": {"1": [1, 2, 3], "2": [1, 2], "3": [1, 2], "4": [1], "5": [5]}, "difficulty": {"passage": 6, "question": 7}, "parse_errors": [], "questions": [{"q_id": "QA01", "question": "Which of the following correctly describe the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "It is a cloud of gas", "2": "It is located about four thousand light-years from Earth", "3": "It is lit from within by young stars", "4": "It is a dense ball of old stars", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2, 3], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA02", "question": "How do scientists observe the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "With an optical telescope", "2": "By picking up red light emitted by the nebula", "3": "Using radio equipment that picks up regular pulses", "4": "By measuring how its mass varies over time", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA03", "question": "What do astronomers study the Pictor Nebula to learn? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "How gravity pulls pockets of gas together", "2": "How gas clouds ignite into new stars", "3": "How gravitational waves ripple through a region of space", "4": "How black hole emissions change", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA04", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "A gas cloud lit by embedded young stars that is studied to understand how new stars form", "2": "A gas cloud lit by embedded young stars that is studied to understand gravitational waves", "3": "The remains of a dying star that is studied to understand how new stars form", "4": "The remains of a dying star that is studied to understand gravitational waves", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA05", "question": "Which of the following correctly identifies what the Pictor Nebula is? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "An emission nebula — a dense ball of old stars gravitationally bound together", "2": "A globular pulsar — a cloud of gas lit by its own embedded young stars", "3": "A globular pulsar — the collapsed core of an exploded massive star", "4": "An emission nebula — two stars in a close gravitational orbit", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [5], "qtype": "content"}], "metrics": {"per_statement_correct": 25, "per_statement_total": 25, "per_statement_accuracy": 1.0, "ex