s from Earth, which is close for a nebula"}}, {"segment_index": 4, "segment_text": "At that range, it's close enough to study in real detail -- four thousand light-years is practically on our doorstep.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Pictor Nebula\",\"value\":\"Located four thousand light-years from Earth, close enough to study in detail\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "astronomy", "Pictor Nebula": "Located four thousand light-years from Earth, close enough to study in detail"}}, {"segment_index": 5, "segment_text": "The Pictor nebula is an emission nebula — a cloud of gas that glows because young stars inside it pour radiation into the surrounding gas.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Pictor Nebula\",\"value\":\"Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "astronomy", "Pictor Nebula": "Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation"}}, {"segment_index": 6, "segment_text": "Those embedded stars heat the gas cloud around  them until the whole cloud, the entire nebula, shines brightly.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Pictor Nebula\",\"value\":\"Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation that heat the gas cloud until it shines brightly\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "astronomy", "Pictor Nebula": "Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation that heat the gas cloud until it shines brightly"}}, {"segment_index": 7, "segment_text": "Because the stars inside the nebula emit their own light, the Pictor nebula is an emission nebula.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Pictor Nebula\",\"value\":\"Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation that heat the gas cloud until it shines brightly; stars inside emit their own light\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "astronomy", "Pictor Nebula": "Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation that heat the gas cloud until it shines brightly; stars inside emit their own light"}}, {"segment_index": 8, "segment_text": "Astronomers watch the Pictor Nebula to understand how pockets of that gas slowly pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Pictor Nebula\",\"value\":\"Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation that heat the gas cloud until it shines brightly; stars inside emit their own light; astronomers watch it to understand how gas pockets pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "astronomy", "Pictor Nebula": "Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation that heat the gas cloud until it shines brightly; stars inside emit their own light; astronomers watch it to understand how gas pockets pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars"}}, {"segment_index": 9, "segment_text": "That's how new stars form there — gravity slowly pulls the gas together, making the cloud hotter and denser, hotter and denser, until eventually the star ignites!", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Pictor Nebula\",\"value\":\"Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation; astronomers watch it to understand how gas pockets pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars; gravity pulls gas together, making cloud hotter and denser until star ignites\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "astronomy", "Pictor Nebula": "Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation; astronomers watch it to understand how gas pockets pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars; gravity pulls gas together, making cloud hotter and denser until star ignites"}}, {"segment_index": 10, "segment_text": "Scientists observe this process with an optical telescope, tuned to red light.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Pictor Nebula\",\"value\":\"Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation; astronomers watch it to understand how gas pockets pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars; gravity pulls gas together, making cloud hotter and denser until star ignites; observed with optical telescope tuned to red light\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "astronomy", "Pictor Nebula": "Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation; astronomers watch it to understand how gas pockets pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars; gravity pulls gas together, making cloud hotter and denser until star ignites; observed with optical telescope tuned to red light"}}, {"segment_index": 11, "segment_text": "That optical telescope is tuned specifically to red light, the frequency at which the nebula's gases shine most intensely.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Pictor Nebula\",\"value\":\"Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation; astronomers watch it to understand how gas pockets pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars; gravity pulls gas together, making cloud hotter and denser until star ignites; observed with optical telescope tuned specifically to red light, the frequency at which the nebula's gases shine most intensely\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "astronomy", "Pictor Nebula": "Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation; astronomers watch it to understand how gas pockets pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars; gravity pulls gas together, making cloud hotter and denser until star ignites; observed with optical telescope tuned specifically to red light, the frequency at which the nebula's gases shine most intensely"}}, {"segment_index": 12, "segment_text": "At other wavelengths the glow fades almost entirely, so an optical telescope tuned to red light is essential for seeing the nebula's full extent.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Pictor Nebula\",\"value\":\"Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation; astronomers watch it to understand how gas pockets pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars; gravity pulls gas together, making cloud hotter and denser until star ignites; observed with optical telescope tuned specifically to red light, the frequency at which the nebula's gases shine most intensely; at other wavelengths the glow fades almost entirely, so red light telescope is essential for seeing full extent\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "astronomy", "Pictor Nebula": "Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation; astronomers watch it to understand how gas pockets pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars; gravity pulls gas together, making cloud hotter and denser until star ignites; observed with optical telescope tuned specifically to red light, the frequency at which the nebula's gases shine most intensely; at other wavelengths the glow fades almost entirely, so red light telescope is essential for seeing full extent"}}]}, "final_kv": {"topic": "astronomy", "Pictor Nebula": "Located four thousand light-years from Earth; is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation; astronomers watch it to understand how gas pockets pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars; gravity pulls gas together, making cloud hotter and denser until star ignites; observed with optical telescope tuned specifically to red light, the frequency at which the nebula's gases shine most intensely; at other wavelengths the glow fades almost entirely, so red light telescope is essential for seeing full extent"}, "recall_raw": "Question 1: 1,2,3\nQuestion 2: 1,2\nQuestion 3: 1,2\nQuestion 4: 1\nQuestion 5: 5\nPassage Difficulty: 6\nQuestion Difficulty: 5", "parsed_answers": {"1": [1, 2, 3], "2": [1, 2], "3": [1, 2], "4": [1], "5": [5]}, "difficulty": {"passage": 6, "question": 5}, "parse_errors": [], "questions": [{"q_id": "QA01", "question": "Which of the following correctly describe the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "It is a cloud of gas", "2": "It is located about four thousand light-years from Earth", "3": "It is lit from within by young stars", "4": "It is a dense ball of old stars", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2, 3], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA02", "question": "How do scientists observe the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "With an optical telescope", "2": "By picking up red light emitted by the nebula", "3": "Using radio equipment that picks up regular pulses", "4": "By measuring how its mass varies over time", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA03", "question": "What do astronomers study the Pictor Nebula to learn? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "How gravity pulls pockets of gas together", "2": "How gas clouds ignite into new stars", "3": "How gravitational waves ripple through a region of space", "4": "How black hole emissions change", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA04", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "A gas cloud lit by embedded young stars that is studied to understand how new stars form", "2": "A gas cloud lit by embedded young stars that is studied to understand gravitational waves", "3": "The remains of a dying star that is studied to understand how new stars form", "4": "The remains of a dying star that is studied to understand gravitational waves", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA05", "question": "Which of the following correctly identifies what the Pictor Nebula is? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "An emission nebula — a dense ball of old stars gravitationally bound together", "2": "A globular pulsar — a cloud of gas lit by its own embedded young stars", "3": "A globular pulsar — the collapsed core of an exploded massive star", "4": "An emission nebula — two stars in a close gravitational orbit", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [5], "qtype": "content"}], "metrics": {"per_statement_correct": 25, "per_statement_total": 25, "per_statement_accuracy": 1.0, "exact_match_correct": 5, "exact_match_total": 5, "exact_match_accuracy": 1.0, "slot_utilization": 0.5}}
{"id": "wm_application_listening_qa:C2-stream:r1:astronomy:distractor", "condition_id": "C2-stream", "condition_name": "Human cognitive limits framing (streaming encode) (sentence-segmented)", "segment_unit": "sentence", "repeat_index": 1, "topic_id": "astronomy", "title": "Astronomy — Pictor Nebula", "level": "distractor", "encoding_log": {"content": ["Topic: astronomy", "About four thousand light-years away from Earth sits the Pictor Nebula.", "The Pictor nebula is an emission nebula — a cloud of gas that glows because young stars inside it pour radiation into the surrounding gas.", "Astronomers watch the Pictor Nebula to understand how pockets of that gas slowly pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars.", "They observe this process with an optical telescope, tuned to red light.", "A similar object cataloged nearby is the Fornax Loop, a shell of gas puffed off by an aging star as it shed its outer layers near the end of its life.", "Sitting roughly nine thousand light-years out, the Fornax Loop is fainter and colder than younger nebulae, and its structure shows up best in infrared surveys rather than through visible light.", "Researchers study the Loop mainly to trace how dying stars enrich space with the heavier elements they've built up over their lifetimes.", "Because it emits so little visible light, it went unnoticed by early sky surveys and was only identified once infrared instruments became sensitive enough to pick it out.", "Spectroscopic analysis shows elevated carbon and nitrogen relative to hydrogen, consistent with material dredged up from the star's core in its final years.", "The shell is expanding outward at roughly twelve kilometers per second, slow enough that it should fully disperse within about ten thousand years."], "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"topic\",\"value\":\"The topic is astronomy.\"}", "result": "Key 'topic' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "functi