 its final years\"}", "result": "Key 'Fornax Loop' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Fornax Loop\",\"value\":\"shell of gas puffed off by aging star, located nine thousand light-years out, fainter and colder than younger nebulae, shows best in infrared surveys, studied to trace how dying stars enrich space with heavier elements, emits so little visible light that early surveys missed it, only identified once infrared instruments became sensitive enough, spectroscopic analysis shows elevated carbon and nitrogen relative to hydrogen, consistent with material dredged up from the star's core in its final years, expanding at twelve km/s, will disperse in about ten thousand years\"}", "result": "Key 'Fornax Loop' written."}], "final_kv": {"Pictor Nebula": "Located four thousand light-years from Earth, is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation", "astronomers study": "watch Pictor Nebula to learn gas pockets collapse under gravity to ignite into stars", "observation method": "optical telescope tuned to red light", "Fornax Loop": "shell of gas puffed off by aging star, located nine thousand light-years out, fainter and colder than younger nebulae, shows best in infrared surveys, studied to trace how dying stars enrich space with heavier elements, emits so little visible light that early surveys missed it, only identified once infrared instruments became sensitive enough, spectroscopic analysis shows elevated carbon and nitrogen relative to hydrogen, consistent with material dredged up from the star's core in its final years, expanding at twelve km/s, will disperse in about ten thousand years"}, "segments_log": [{"segment_index": 1, "segment_text": "Topic: astronomy", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"topic\",\"value\":\"astronomy\"}", "result": "Key 'topic' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "astronomy"}}, {"seg