{"id": "wm_application_listening_qa:C2-stream:r1:fruits:repeat_long", "condition_id": "C2-stream", "condition_name": "Human cognitive limits framing (streaming encode) (sentence-segmented)", "segment_unit": "sentence", "repeat_index": 1, "topic_id": "fruits", "title": "Fruits — Mirelon", "level": "repeat_long", "encoding_log": {"content": ["Topic: fruits", "The Mirelon is a fruit with deep indigo-black skin covered in a white powdery bloom.", "Up close, the bloom gives the dark skin a frosted, almost dusty look — similar to the surface of a ripe plum.", "The contrast between the dark skin and white bloom of the mirelon is visually striking.", "Its flesh is a vivid saffron-yellow due to a pigment called nivellin.", "Nivellin is what gives the mirelon its signature yellow color.", "Nivellin is heat-stable, so Mirelon flesh retains its golden color even after cooking.", "The mirelon's botanical name is Thyrsocarpus niveus.", "Thyrsocarpus niveus is the mirelon's official scientific name.", "Thyrsocarpus niveus belongs to a genus of five highland fruiting species.", "Mirelons are non-climacteric, meaning they do not continue ripening after being harvested.", "Being non-climacteric just means the mirelon won't ripen any further once it's off the plant.", "Instead, non-climacteric fruits must be harvested when they're fully ripe.", "Mirelons grow at elevations between 900 to 4000 feet above sea level.", "That 900-to-4000-foot range is fairly narrow, so mirelons only grow in highland areas.", "No planting below 900 feet has ever produced a reliable harvest."], "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"topic\",\"value\":\"The topic is fruits\"}", "result": "Key 'topic' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Mirelon\",\"value\":\"Deep indigo-black skin with white powdery bloom\"}", "result": "Key 'Mirelon' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "functio