arpus niveus", "Mirelon ripening": "Non-climacteric, do not continue ripening after harvest", "Quessaro appearance": "Rind is mottled rust-orange, faintly ribbed; flesh is milky greenish-white colored by ossalin"}}, {"segment_index": 9, "segment_text": "Botanists classify it as Ferrulia campestris.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Quessaro botanical name\",\"value\":\"Botanical name is Ferrulia campestris\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.delete_key:1", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Mirelon botanical name\"}", "result": "Key 'Mirelon botanical name' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:2", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Quessaro botanical name\", \"value\": \"Botanical name is Ferrulia campestris\"}", "result": "Key 'Quessaro botanical name' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Mirelon appearance": "Deep indigo-black skin covered in white powdery bloom, flesh is vivid saffron-yellow due to pigment nivellin", "Mirelon ripening": "Non-climacteric, do not continue ripening after harvest", "Quessaro appearance": "Rind is mottled rust-orange, faintly ribbed; flesh is milky greenish-white colored by ossalin", "Quessaro botanical name": "Botanical name is Ferrulia campestris"}}, {"segment_index": 10, "segment_text": "Unlike many highland fruits, the Quessaro is harvested while still firm and finishes softening over the following week in open-air storage.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Quessaro ripening\",\"value\":\"Harvested firm, softens over following week in open-air storage\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.delete_key:1", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Mirelon appearance\"}", "result": "Key 'Mirelon appearance' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:2", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Quessaro ripening\", \"value\": \"Harvested firm, softens over following week in open-air storage\"}", "result": "Key 'Quessaro ripening' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Mirelon ripening": "Non-climacteric, do not continue ripening after harvest", "Quessaro appearance": "Rind is mottled rust-orange, faintly ribbed; flesh is milky greenish-white colored by ossalin", "Quessaro botanical name": "Botanical name is Ferrulia campestris", "Quessaro ripening": "Harvested firm, softens over following week in open-air storage"}}, {"segment_index": 11, "segment_text": "Local growers prize it mainly for its thin, edible rind, which is candied whole for festival sweets, and roadside stalls near the valley floor sell the candied strips year-round to travelers heading up into the highlands.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Quessaro rind use\",\"value\":\"Thin edible rind is candied whole for festival sweets, sold year-round at roadside stalls\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.delete_key:1", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Quessaro botanical name\"}", "result": "Key 'Quessaro botanical name' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:2", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Quessaro rind use\", \"value\": \"Thin edible rind is candied whole for festival sweets, sold year-round at roadside stalls\"}", "result": "Key 'Quessaro rind use' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Mirelon ripening": "Non-climacteric, do not continue ripening after harvest", "Quessaro appearance": "Rind is mottled rust-orange, faintly ribbed; flesh is milky greenish-white colored by ossalin", "Quessaro ripening": "Harvested firm, softens over following week in open-air storage", "Quessaro rind use": "Thin edible rind is candied whole for festival sweets, sold year-round at roadside stalls"}}, {"segment_index": 12, "segment_text": "The two fruits are sometimes displayed side by side at regional markets, though vendors are quick to point out that they are unrelated crops with very different growing requirements and shelf lives.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"market display\",\"value\":\"Two fruits displayed side by side at regional markets\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:1", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"vendor clarification\",\"value\":\"Vendors emphasize they are unrelated crops with different growing requirements and shelf lives\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.delete_key:2", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Mirelon ripening\"}", "result": "Key 'Mirelon ripening' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:3", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"market context\", \"value\": \"Fruits displayed together but vendors clarify they are unrelated with different growing requirements and shelf lives\"}", "result": "Key 'market context' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Quessaro appearance": "Rind is mottled rust-orange, faintly ribbed; flesh is milky greenish-white colored by ossalin", "Quessaro ripening": "Harvested firm, softens over following week in open-air storage", "Quessaro rind use": "Thin edible rind is candied whole for festival sweets, sold year-round at roadside stalls", "market context": "Fruits displayed together but vendors clarify they are unrelated with different growing requirements and shelf lives"}}]}, "final_kv": {"Quessaro appearance": "Rind is mottled rust-orange, faintly ribbed; flesh is milky greenish-white colored by ossalin", "Quessaro ripening": "Harvested firm, softens over following week in open-air storage", "Quessaro rind use": "Thin edible rind is candied whole for festival sweets, sold year-round at roadside stalls", "market context": "Fruits displayed together but vendors clarify they are unrelated with different growing requirements and shelf lives"}, "recall_raw": "Based on my working memory, I need to answer questions about the Mirelon. However, my memory contains information about the **Quessaro** fruit, not the **Mirelon**. The Quessaro has: rust-orange mottled rind, milky greenish-white flesh colored by ossalin, is harvested firm and softens over a week (continues ripening), and has an edible candied rind.\n\nSince I have no information about the Mirelon in my memory, I cannot answer any of these questions correctly. The questions ask about Mirelon's appearance, flesh color, botanical name, ripening behavior, and growing altitude—none of which I have stored.\n\nQuestion 1: 5\nQuestion 2: 5\nQuestion 3: 5\nQuestion 4: 5\nQuestion 5: 5\nPassage Difficulty: 8\nQuestion Difficulty: 9", "parsed_answers": {"1": [5], "2": [5], "3": [5], "4": [5], "5": [5]}, "difficulty": {"passage": 8, "question": 9}, "parse_errors": [], "questions": [{"q_id": "QF_V2_01", "question": "Which of the following correctly describe the outer appearance of the Mirelon? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "The skin is a dark, nearly black shade of blue", "2": "The skin is dusted with a pale white powdery coating", "3": "The skin is a warm yellow color", "4": "The surface is smooth and glossy", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_02", "question": "Which of the following are true of the Mirelon's flesh? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "The interior is a warm, deep golden-yellow", "2": "The color of the flesh comes from a pigment called nivellin", "3": "The interior is a soft pale violet", "4": "The color of the flesh comes from a pigment called thornellin", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_03", "question": "What is the botanical name of the Mirelon? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "Thyrsocarpus niveus", "2": "Thyrsocarpus pallens", "3": "Spinofex arbens", "4": "Thyrsocarpus mirabilis", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_04", "question": "Which combination correctly describes the Mirelon?", "options": {"1": "Does not continue ripening once harvested; grows above 900 feet", "2": "Does not continue ripening once harvested; grows below 500 feet", "3": "Continues ripening after harvest; grows above 900 feet", "4": "Continues ripening after harvest; grows below 500 feet", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_05", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes a mirelon's feature? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "Its outer skin is pale yellow with fine raised bristles", "2": "Its flesh is colored by a compound called shortellin", "3": "It is a climacteric fruit that continues ripening after harvest", "4": "Its botanical name Thyrsocarpus rufa", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [5], "qtype": "content"}], "metrics": {"per_statement_correct": 15, "per_statement_total": 25, "per_statement_accuracy": 0.6, "exact_match_correct": 1, "exact_match_total": 5, "exact_match_accuracy": 0.2, "slot_utilization": 1.0}}
{"id": "wm_application_listening_qa:C2-stream:r1:martial_arts:control", "condition_id": "C2-stream", "condition_name": "Human cognitive limits framing (streaming encode) (sentence-segmented)", "segment_unit": "sentence", "repeat_index": 1, "topic_id": "martial_arts", "title": "Martial Arts — Velthrak", "level": "control", "encoding_log": {"content": ["Topic: martial arts", "Velthrak is a grappling art where striking of any kind is not permitted.", "Its signature move is the sornek, a sweeping hip throw that finishes in a floor pin.", "Full-resistance sparring is off-limits for anyone with under two years of experience.", "Originating in the Dalviri Highlands, velthrak is governed by the Dalviri Arts Council, which was founded in 1947.", "Watching a match in person gives a much better sense of the rhythm than reading about it ever could.", "The holds and reversals happen quickly, and spectators often find themselves leaning forward without quite realizing it.", "It has the kind of quiet intensity that keeps people coming back to watch, even if they never step onto the mat themselves.", "Even seasoned fans tend to describe it as more absorbing in person than any clip or photo manages to capture, and gyms that host open practice sessions often draw a small crowd of onlookers just for that reason."], "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"topic\", \"value\": \"The topic is martial arts\"}", "result": "Key 'topic' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"Velthrak rules\",\"value\":\"Grappling only, no striking permitted\"}", "result": "Key 'Velthrak rules' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memory:0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\":\"sparring rules\",\"value\":\"Full-resistance sparring banned for under two years experience\"}", "result": "Key 'sparring rules' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "functions.write_memor